ffs while Rust↔C shows only 5,926, so my translation is closer to each C build than the C builds are to each other. Not a specifiable behavior.\n2. **`c2GJK` with an out-of-range cache** made the C read uninitialized stack (my first harness seeded bogus caches and saw 41k C-vs-C diffs across opt levels). I re-scoped those tests to in-range indices plus realistic warm-start chains; C's behavior on bogus caches is genuinely nondeterministic. Note my Rust zero-initializes `c2Proxy`/`c2Simplex` where C leaves garbage — the only reachable divergence, and only on inputs where C is already undefined.\n\nPer instructions I reproduced quirks rather than fixing them: `c2GJKSimplexMetric`'s `default:` fallthrough into `case 1`, the inverted cache-validity test (`!(min < max*2 && metric < -1.0e8f)`, whose second clause is essentially always false), `c2Collided`'s argument-swapping for mixed type pairs, and the unset `u` field on newly added simplex vertices. `c_src/` was not modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1295,"cache_read_input_tokens":80250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1295,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"043bc660-c949-4ca6-a48c-8710a385db31","uuid":"e009cb5d-ad22-4a47-a37f-05bb897126d2","timestamp":"2026-08-20T04:42:38.659Z"}
